{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.AlgebraMap","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Kronecker","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.kz_formal_solutions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.kz_formal_solutions","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L303-L314","doc":"**The three-point `𝔤𝔩_n` KZ system has a unique normalised formal solution at `z = 0`**\n(residue `A = ℏ P₁₂`) **and at `z = 1`** (residue `B = ℏ P₂₃`, after `w = 1 − z`, which swaps\nthe roles of `A` and `B`), whenever `ℏ` is not rational. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.kzM0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.kzM0","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L298-L301","doc":"The coefficient sequence of `z · (A/z + B/(z−1)) = A − B ∑_{k≥1} z^k` at `z = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P23_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P23_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L295-L296","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P12_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P12_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L292-L293","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P23","kind":"def","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L290-L290","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.P12","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L288-L289","doc":"`P₁₂` and `P₂₃` on `V^{⊗3}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.swap23","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.swap23","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L285-L286","doc":"The flip of the last two factors of `V^{⊗3}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.swap12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.swap12","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L282-L283","doc":"The flip of the first two factors of `V^{⊗3}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.casimir_eq_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.casimir_eq_flip","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L274-L280","doc":"**The `𝔤𝔩_n` Casimir on `V ⊗ V` is the flip.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.casimir2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.casimir2","kind":"def","line":269,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L269-L272","doc":"The `𝔤𝔩_n` Casimir `Ω = ∑_{a,b} E_{ab} ⊗ E_{ba}` (trace form) on `V ⊗ V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.flip2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.flip2","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L266-L267","doc":"The flip on `V ⊗ V`, `V = K^n`, as a matrix indexed by `Fin n × Fin n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.single_apply'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.single_apply'","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L263-L264","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.permMat_mul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.permMat_mul_self","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L257-L261","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.permMat_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.permMat_mul","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L252-L255","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.permMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.permMat","kind":"def","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L248-L250","doc":"The permutation matrix of `σ`: column `j` is the basis vector `e_{σ j}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.nonResonant_smul_involution_of_irrational","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.nonResonant_smul_involution_of_irrational","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L230-L238","doc":"**Irrational coupling is non-resonant.** If `ℏ` is not the image of a rational, then `ℏ P`\nis non-resonant for every involution `P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.nonResonant_smul_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.nonResonant_smul_involution","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L222-L228","doc":"**Non-resonance for `ℏ P`, `P² = 1`**: it suffices that `k² ≠ 4ℏ²` for every integer `k ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.aeval_adL_smul_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.aeval_adL_smul_involution","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L207-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.ad_cube_of_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.ad_cube_of_involution","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L198-L203","doc":"For an involution `P`, `ad_P³ = 4 ad_P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.nonResonant_of_aeval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.nonResonant_of_aeval","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L185-L190","doc":"**Non-resonance from an annihilating polynomial of `ad_A`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.indicial_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.indicial_eq","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L178-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.adL_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.adL_apply","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L176-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.adL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.adL","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L173-L174","doc":"`ad_A` as a `K`-linear endomorphism of `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.isUnit_algebraMap_sub_of_aeval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.isUnit_algebraMap_sub_of_aeval","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L152-L169","doc":"**Resolvent from an annihilating polynomial.** In an algebra over a field, if `p(T) = 0` and\n`p(k) ≠ 0`, then `k − T` is a unit; its inverse is `q(T)/p(k)` where\n`p − p(k) = (X − k) q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.exists_unique_formalGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.exists_unique_formalGauge","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L140-L146","doc":"**Existence and uniqueness** of the normalised formal solution at a non-resonant\nregular singular point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalGauge_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalGauge_unique","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L123-L138","doc":"**Uniqueness**: two formal solutions with `H₀ = 1` agree, given injectivity of the indicial\noperators (half of non-resonance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalSol_isFormalGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalSol_isFormalGauge","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L118-L121","doc":"**Existence** of a formal solution with `H₀ = 1` under non-resonance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.indicial_formalSol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.indicial_formalSol","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L109-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalSol_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalSol_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L106-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalSol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.formalSol","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L99-L104","doc":"The formal solution, built by recursion from the inverses of the indicial operators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.isFormalGauge_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.isFormalGauge_iff","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L81-L97","doc":"With `H₀ = 1`, the gauge equation is exactly the indicial recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.IsFormalGauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.IsFormalGauge","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L77-L79","doc":"`H` is a formal solution of the gauge equation `z H' + H M₀ = M H`, coefficientwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.NonResonant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.NonResonant","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L73-L75","doc":"**Non-resonance at the singular point**: every indicial operator with `k ≥ 1` is bijective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.indicial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.indicial","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L70-L71","doc":"The `k`-th indicial operator `X ↦ k X − ad_A X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.ad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KZ.FuchsianFormal.ad","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KZ/FuchsianFormal.lean#L67-L68","doc":"The commutator `ad_A X = A X − X A`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}